.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt ASN1_OBJECT_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ASN1_OBJECT_new ,
.Nm ASN1_OBJECT_free
.Nd object allocation functions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/asn1.h
.Ft ASN1_OBJECT *
.Fo ASN1_OBJECT_new
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo ASN1_OBJECT_free
.Fa "ASN1_OBJECT *a"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Vt ASN1_OBJECT
allocation routines, allocate and free an
.Vt ASN1_OBJECT
structure, which represents an ASN1 OBJECT IDENTIFIER.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_OBJECT_new
allocates and initializes an
.Vt ASN1_OBJECT
structure.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_OBJECT_free
frees up the
.Vt ASN1_OBJECT
structure
.Fa a .
If
.Fa a
is NULL, nothing is done.
.Sh NOTES
Although
.Fn ASN1_OBJECT_new
allocates a new
.Vt ASN1_OBJECT
structure it is almost never used in applications.
The ASN1 object utility functions such as
.Xr OBJ_nid2obj 3
are used instead.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
If the allocation fails,
.Fn ASN1_OBJECT_new
returns NULL and sets an error code that can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
Otherwise it returns a pointer to the newly allocated structure.
.Pp
.Fn ASN1_OBJECT_free
returns no value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr d2i_ASN1_OBJECT 3
